    "what_this_means": "Jeff McNeil kept the lineup afloat with three RBI, but it was Tommy White's single in the eighth that sparked the actual swing. Three runs that proved the difference in an 8-3 win over Texas. The Athletics trailed early chaos in the sixth when Texas scored three to tie it up, but they never actually ceded control of the game. McNeil's power early in the first (3 runs, go-ahead) meant Texas had to chase from the start. The critical test came in those empty middle innings. The second and fifth innings with runners in scoring position where nothing landed. The bullpen held clean through the middle frames. Medina struck out two in 1.1 scoreless. Rom and Alvarado each logged a clean strikeout. Then the eighth broke open: White's single, three runs across, and the game was decided on the spot. This is a team that doesn't need early separation to win tight games. They can break you late if the foundation holds.",
